11. Min Stack (getMin() in O(1))

Idea

Maintain two stacks:

- Main Stack → Stores all elements.
- Min Stack → Stores only the minimum element at each stage.

Whenever a new element is pushed:

- Push it into the main stack.
- If it is smaller than or equal to the current minimum, also push it into the min stack.

Whenever an element is popped:

- If it is equal to the top of the min stack, remove it from both stacks.

The minimum element is always available at the top of the min stack.

Push: 5
Min = 5

Push: 3
Min = 3

Push: 7
Min = 3

Pop()
Min = 3

Pop()
Min = 5

Complexities

- Push → O(1)
- Pop → O(1)
- getMin() → O(1)

