15. Reverse a Queue Using a Stack

Algorithm

1. Create an empty stack.
2. Remove each element from the queue and push it onto the stack.
3. Pop all elements from the stack and insert them back into the queue.
4. The queue is now reversed.

C Program

#include <stdio.h>

int main() {

    int queue[] = {10, 20, 30, 40};
    int stack[10];
    int top = -1;
    int n = 4;

    // Push queue elements into stack
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
        stack[++top] = queue[i];

    // Pop back into queue
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
        queue[i] = stack[top--];

    printf("Reversed Queue: ");

    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
        printf("%d ", queue[i]);

    return 0;
}

Output

Reversed Queue: 40 30 20 10

Time Complexity: O(n)

Space Complexity: O(n)

