1. Infix to Postfix Conversion

Expression

A + B * (C - D) / E

Algorithm

START

Create an empty stack.

Scan the infix expression from left to right.

If the symbol is an operand,
    Add it to the postfix expression.

Else if the symbol is '(',
    Push it onto the stack.

Else if the symbol is ')',
    Pop and append operators until '(' is found.
    Remove '('.

Else if the symbol is an operator,
    While the stack is not empty and the top operator has
    higher or equal precedence,
        Pop and append it.
    Push the current operator.

After scanning the expression,
Pop all remaining operators.

STOP

Stack Table

Symbol| Stack| Postfix
A| -| A
+| +| A
B| +| AB
*| + *| AB
(| + * (| AB
C| + * (| ABC
-| + * ( -| ABC
D| + * ( -| ABCD
)| + *| ABCD-
/| + /| ABCD-*
E| + /| ABCD-*E
End| -| *ABCD-E/+

Final Answer

ABCD-*E/+

Time Complexity: O(n)

